{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And Joshua weakened Amalek.</b> The Amalekites practiced sorcery so that the sword would not have power over them to kill; therefore Israel struck them and weakened them with the sword but did not kill them. Another interpretation: because above it is written 'and Amalek prevailed,' here it writes 'and he weakened'; but in any case it is an expression of killing, as in 'the mighty man dies and is undone' (וגבר ימות ויחלש)."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:58:20.400256183Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}